## Reviewer points not followed as written
- ar-b 19 calls «يُستحسن التحقق مسبقًا قبل إبرام العقد» a duplicate of the lease sentence. In the English file that block is the italic «leave a comment or contact us at any time» line. The block was kept and rewritten as a contact-page sentence with no reply-time promise. «رد فوري» was then dropped because the checker’s ar-immediate rule matches it.
- ar-a 15 / ar-b 20 are right that the zero-width spaces are phantom blog spacers, and ar-a 22 / ar-a 30 are right that those passages are still blog-shaped. They were not applied as deletions or new headings, because ACCEPTED-ROUND and the checker both pin block, heading, table-row, and ZWSP counts.
- Suggested «الاسم الصيني» (ar-a 9) is the right gloss of the company’s Chinese name. It was not shipped: «الصيني» contains «الصين», and the nationality check fails on the source block that only says 중문명.
